  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 39,
    "summary": "Man’s weakness and ignorance are compared with God’s mighty works—Does man even know how the laws of nature operate?",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Knowest thou the time when the wild goats of the rock bring forth? or canst thou mark when the hinds do calve?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Nature, Earth."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Nature, Earth.",
            "prettyString": "TG Nature, Earth",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Nature, Earth",
                "entryId": "tg-nature-earth",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Canst thou number the months that they fulfil? or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "They bow themselves, they bring forth their young ones, they cast out their sorrows.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Their young ones are in good liking, they grow up with corn; they go forth, and return not unto them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Who hath sent out the wild ass free? or who hath loosed the bands of the wild ass?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose house I have made the wilderness, and the barren land his dwellings.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "He scorneth the multitude of the city, neither regardeth he the crying of the driver.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "The range of the mountains is his pasture, and he searcheth after every green thing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Will the unicorn be willing to serve thee, or abide by thy crib?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "HEB buffalo, bison."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Canst thou bind the unicorn with his band in the furrow? or will he harrow the valleys after thee?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Wilt thou trust him, because his strength is great? or wilt thou leave thy labour to him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Wilt thou believe him, that he will bring home thy seed, and gather it into thy barn?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Gavest thou the goodly wings unto the peacocks? or wings and feathers unto the ostrich?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Which leaveth her eggs in the earth, and warmeth them in dust,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And forgetteth that the foot may crush them, or that the wild beast may break them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "She is hardened against her young ones, as though they were not hers: her labour is in vain without fear;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Lam. 4:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Lam. 4:3.",
            "prettyString": "Lamentations 4:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "lamentations",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Because God hath deprived her of wisdom, neither hath he imparted to her understanding.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "What time she lifteth up herself on high, she scorneth the horse and his rider.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Hast thou given the horse strength? hast thou clothed his neck with thunder?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Canst thou make him afraid as a grasshopper? the glory of his nostrils is terrible.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "He paweth in the valley, and rejoiceth in his strength: he goeth on to meet the armed men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "He mocketh at fear, and is not affrighted; neither turneth he back from the sword.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "The quiver rattleth against him, the glittering spear and the shield.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage: neither believeth he that it is the sound of the trumpet.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha; and he smelleth the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom, and stretch her wings toward the south?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Doth the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest on high?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "She dwelleth and abideth on the rock, upon the crag of the rock, and the strong place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "From thence she seeketh the prey, and her eyes behold afar off.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Her young ones also suck up blood: and where the slain are, there is she.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 39:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 39,
        "verse": 30
      }
    ]
